  "source": "JoyPro curated on the maker's photo (2026-10-11), only the LEFT F/A-18 throttle handle, seen from the side that carries its four controls (top hat, rocker, slide switch, push button), no base and no right handle on the photo",
  "mappingSource": "WinWing \"F18 HANDLE + T1 SUPER TAURUS THROTTLE BASE User manual V1.1\" section 2.1 \"F18-TGRIP-L\\F18-TGRIP-R\" drawing, page 10 (https://en.winwing.cn/static/file/T1-SUPER%20TARUS%20THROTTLE%20BASE-MANUAL%20EN%20V%201.1.pdf): upper drawing (this handle) 1 = hat 8-12, 2 = hat 13-17, 3 = switch 18/19/20, 4 = button 21; lower drawing (right handle) 5 = ministick 22 + X/Y, 6 = Z wheel, 7 = button 7, 8 = button 6, 9 = toggle 3/4/5",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "note": "The right handle (ministick, Z wheel, buttons 6/7 and the 3/4/5 toggle that the catalog calls \"Speed brake\") is not on this photo; the throttle.base.* parts are the Orion 2 base's, also not shown. Buttons 18/19/20 (catalog throttle.button.1-3) are the three positions of the one slide switch 3; which end is 18 vs 20 is not shown in the drawing. Catalog naming doubt: the long toggle 3/4/5 is on the RIGHT handle (where the real F/A-18 has the exterior lights switch), while the left handle's slide switch 18-20 sits where the real speed brake switch is.",
